# Instruction guards from thread-index predicates: stores under and,
# or and not of %tid.x comparisons count their guarded threads per
# CTA (1, 32, 32, 63), the branch on the and.pred selects the
# fallthrough block for the other 63, and the guard on a loaded value
# keeps the store total a bound.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/guards.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
CHECK: kernel micro_guards
CHECK: |    <block 1>  (no line info)       1  63 in 2 warps (not (%tid.x == 0 and %tid.x < 32))  $L__BB0_2
CHECK: block size: 64 threads, 2 warps (64x1x1 from .reqntid)
CHECK: <block 0>  ld.global.f32     global load 4 B                                                        warp: 4–5 sectors (ideal 4)    [4 * %tid.x + param_0]
CHECK: <block 0>  ld.global.f32     global load 4 B on 1 thread in 1 warp (%tid.x == 0 and %tid.x < 32)    warp: 1 sector (ideal 1)       [4 * %tid.x + param_0 + 512]
CHECK: totals per CTA [static]:
CHECK: global store 8 B      127
CHECK: st.global.b64        63
CHECK: global bytes: load 516 B, store <= 1730 B
